{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788589166326320009,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unvagrant-venomous-mara","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"6d4975d15a238166ea8749236f54ba5a604775f702e7184093c6603d9b79c1aa","event_uuid":"42593dfe-eac7-42f4-9885-958eb8a1accc","position":{"commit_sha":"47302bcf5731f691c2feac897dcdd05da6b02850","position":"1788584356161556001-42593dfe-eac7-42f4-9885-958eb8a1accc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"56370ee72122daebfa4cd5dc26cb0d79bf3b993b29bc72fddbd9e61a85a8203e","event_uuid":"be0a1e1d-348e-44fc-8e71-a0040018e01d","position":{"commit_sha":"490afa78b0a1d6bb027c59c8d9dda3e0482208b8","position":"1788584396730085001-be0a1e1d-348e-44fc-8e71-a0040018e01d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e9ae94797377143ad65a9fb0872f16649a689e0f2e04fdc6c9abc346865e8c0d","event_uuid":"1d5568fa-af4a-4673-886c-8c90bddd3058","position":{"commit_sha":"0057d63f50bb500f69a2cac44f0469a9f294dbe2","position":"1788584441524746001-1d5568fa-af4a-4673-886c-8c90bddd3058"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"60ab1a6983ec7536b2f0b6797d59a3b6587cbceb807928babfe6eb449ffa7604","event_uuid":"3da7d29e-da33-4205-a115-f2b19debf913","position":{"commit_sha":"de38fa7fe8d51d93f90b4a3894c7a09bb6365fcb","position":"1788584672103274001-3da7d29e-da33-4205-a115-f2b19debf913"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator decision recorded — bridge NOT resumed, and why.\n\nStanding rule from the operator: resume a paused bridge only if the pause is older than 24 hours; otherwise assume another session owns it.\n\nMeasured at decision time:\n\n    paused_at  2026-09-05T04:32:38Z\n    now        2026-09-05T05:00:24Z\n    age        27.8 minutes (0.46 h)  ->  older than 24h: FALSE\n\nSo the pause is recent and presumed owned by a concurrent session's `repair:doctor:aca7242c-cd02-411b-931e-37b385f375a7`. Not resumed.\n\nThis is worth recording rather than leaving implicit, because it exposes the operational gap this ticket is about: the ONLY reason a 24-hour rule is applicable here is that `paused_at` happened to be visible in a workflow LOG LINE. `rebar bridge status` returned `\"pause\": null` against a stale pass record minutes later, so had that run not printed `BRIDGE_PAUSED`, the pause age would not have been answerable at all — and the rule could not have been applied.\n\nThat strengthens the third acceptance criterion: `bridge status` must report the CURRENT pause state including its age, because an ownership rule keyed on pause age is unusable without it.","timestamp":1788584441524746001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLARIFICATION to the comment above, to avoid confusing whoever owns that pause.\n\nThat comment records only MY OWN INACTION. It is not a review, adjudication, or claim of ownership over the `repair:doctor:aca7242c-...` pause or the repair behind it.\n\nTo be explicit for the owning session:\n- I did not resume, modify, or interact with the pause in any way.\n- I have no visibility into what the repair is doing and made no judgement about it.\n- Nothing is expected of you in response to that comment, and no decision about your work was taken.\n\nI noted the pause here only because a green workflow run that reconciled nothing is the SUBJECT of this ticket, and that run is the evidence for it. The pause is incidental to the reporting defect; it is not what this ticket is about.\n\nRecording this rather than editing, since the store is append-only and a silent revision would be worse than a visible correction.","timestamp":1788584672103274001}],"created_at":1788584356161556001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"be0a1e1d-348e-44fc-8e71-a0040018e01d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5c5c-5741-9b33-47fa"}],"description":"## The defect\n\nWhen the reconcile bridge is PAUSED, `rebar bridge run` exits 0 and the **Reconcile Bridge\nworkflow reports SUCCESS** — a green run that reconciled nothing. There is no annotation, no\ndistinct status, and nothing in the run's title or conclusion to distinguish \"the Jira/rebar\nreconciler converged\" from \"the reconciler did not execute\".\n\n## Verified by execution, 2026-09-05\n\nRun `33944760258`, conclusion **success**, from its own log:\n\n```\n04:34:47Z  BRIDGE_PAUSED: {\"paused\":true,\n                           \"reason\":\"repair:doctor:aca7242c-cd02-411b-931e-37b385f375a7\",\n                           \"who\":\"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com\",\n                           \"paused_at\":\"2026-09-05T04:32:38Z\"}\n04:34:47Z  Reconciling with bridge profile: live\n04:34:47Z  Reconcile bridge is paused; skipping ticket commit and push.\n```\n\nThe reconciler step began at 04:34:46 and the job completed at 04:34:54 — **eight seconds**,\nagainst roughly twenty-one minutes for a real pass. The four minutes of job wall-clock before that\nare checkout and dependency install, which is why run DURATION alone does not reveal it either.\n\n## What it actually cost — this is not hypothetical\n\nThe bridge had been failing on the ACLI 1200-issue ceiling (`bairnish-sunbeamed-nandine`,\n`5c5c-5741-9b33-47fa`) at 01:33, 02:34 and 03:31. It then reported **success at 04:30**.\n\nI read that green run as recovery, told the operator the outage had \"recovered on its own\", and\nfiled a correction on `5c5c` arguing the failure was INTERMITTENT rather than a permanent\nthreshold crossing. That correction was wrong, and the green run is the entire reason I made it.\nThe implementing agent then measured the active working set per run and showed the crossing is\npermanent:\n\n| run | outcome | active set |\n|---|---|---|\n| 00:59 | success | 1,193 — genuinely under the 1200 ceiling |\n| 01:33 / 02:34 / 03:31 | FAILURE | 1,388 |\n| 04:30 | \"success\" | 1,388 — **paused, no fetch** |\n\nSo the false-green did not merely fail to inform: it actively produced a wrong diagnosis, which\nwas written into a ticket and reported to an operator, and it took a separate measurement pass to\nundo. That is a strictly worse outcome than the workflow having no signal at all.\n\n## Why \"it is only paused, someone knows\" is not a defence\n\nThe pause reason here is `repair:doctor:<uuid>` set by `joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com` — the SHARED\nautomation identity that every concurrent session on this host uses (see\n`carnivoral-puerile-seaurchin`, `8b1c-c577-366b-47d5`). So the pause is not attributable to a\nperson, nothing records when it should end, and no signal exists if it is never lifted. A bridge\npaused indefinitely is a silently-diverging Jira and rebar, reporting green hourly.\n\nNote also that `rebar bridge status` did NOT surface the pause when queried a few minutes later —\nit returned the prior pass's record with `\"pause\": null` and `verdict: FOREIGN`. So the operator's\nobvious \"is the bridge paused?\" query does not reliably answer the question either.\n\n## Directions (none endorsed)\n\n- Publish a `rebar/host:bridge_paused` gauge (1/0) with an alarm that fires when the bridge has\n  been paused beyond some window. This is the shape the repo already uses elsewhere and it makes\n  an indefinite pause page rather than accumulate.\n- Surface the pause in the run itself — a `::warning::`/`::notice::` annotation and a job summary\n  line, so `gh run list` and the Actions UI do not read as an ordinary success.\n- Consider whether a paused pass should be a distinct workflow CONCLUSION rather than success.\n  Exiting non-zero would page on a deliberate pause, which is wrong; a neutral/skipped conclusion\n  or an explicit annotation is likelier the right answer. Decide it, do not default to it.\n- Make `rebar bridge status` answer the pause question directly and currently, rather than\n  returning a possibly-stale pass record whose `pause` field reflects an earlier snapshot.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A paused bridge is DISTINGUISHABLE from a successful reconcile without opening the run log.\n      Proven by pausing a bridge in a non-production environment, running the workflow path, and\n      observing the distinct signal — not by asserting the annotation was added.\n- [ ] An indefinite pause becomes actionable: a pause older than an agreed window produces an\n      alarm or a red signal. Proven by replaying a paused series against the proposed\n      configuration, per the method established in `bff5-9163` AC2, rather than by waiting.\n- [ ] `rebar bridge status` reports the CURRENT pause state, or says plainly that it cannot.\n      Proven by querying it while paused and observing a truthful answer.\n- [ ] Whatever is chosen does NOT page on a short, deliberate operational pause. Record the window\n      and the reasoning; a fix that makes routine maintenance noisy will be disabled and the bug\n      will return.\n- [ ] The existing `bridge_run_failures` semantics are preserved: a healthy pass still publishes 0\n      and a failing pass still publishes 1, so this change adds a signal rather than perturbing\n      the one that already works.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9d8e-872a-8878-4631","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A PAUSED reconcile bridge reports the workflow run as SUCCESS: a green hourly run that reconciled nothing, which produced a wrong diagnosis that reached a ticket and an operator","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["42593dfe-eac7-42f4-9885-958eb8a1accc","be0a1e1d-348e-44fc-8e71-a0040018e01d","1d5568fa-af4a-4673-886c-8c90bddd3058","3da7d29e-da33-4205-a115-f2b19debf913"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788589166326320009,"uuid":"1c62c539-7eac-424e-b18f-a70c5982418c"}